   "widgets_values": [
    "## ACE-Step 1.5 repaint (E18 dev copy) - fill a region, keep the rest\n\n**The audio inpainting route.** A span of a take is silenced, its **latent frames** are masked, and the model\nre-samples only those frames. The geometry is known from `nodes_ace.py`: the audio latent is\n`[batch, 64, seconds x 25]`, so **25 latent frames per second** - 120 s is `[1, 64, 3000]` and this flow masks\nframes **1375..1525** = **55-61 s** (`SolidMask` 0 everywhere, a band of 1s composited at x=1375,\n`SetLatentNoiseMask`, `KSampler` at denoise 1.0 - the **mask** is the region control, so nothing else has to\nbe tuned).\n\n**Input:** `input/ace_iron_gap.flac` - the industrial 'Iron heart' take with 55-61 s silenced (a deliberately\ndeleted piece, so the repair has ground truth to be scored against). **Text:** the take's own style and lyric,\nso the model re-sings the missing words in context.\n\n**After it runs, composite:** the decoded output is VAE round-tripped *everywhere*, so splice the original\ntake's audio back outside the gap (the lesson the image inpaint flow learned). Then compare original / gapped /\nrepaired - the words back in the gap, and everything else untouched.\n"
   ],
   "properties": {},
   "order": 0
  }
